Subject: [PATCH 3/3] P8 round 3: unreadable history, identity, duplicates,
 pagination, human resolution

broker_io.py (proposal, not wired into any bot):
- submit(): unreadable prior history never returns NOT_SUBMITTED; keeps the
  client id, never POSTs, uses read-only broker lookup (ACCEPTED/CONFLICT/
  UNRESOLVED, persisted=False). NOT_SUBMITTED only for readable-empty history.
- identity_mismatches(): symbol/side/type/TIF/qty|notional/limit/stop with
  broker normalization (BTCUSD, decimal formatting); applied to POST responses,
  lookups and scans. Mismatch or >1 order per client id -> CONFLICT.
- Bounded cursor pagination (500/page, max 3 pages, 1us overlap + id dedup);
  truncation/page failure/bound -> incomplete, never absence.
- States CONFLICT and ABANDONED; append-only intent_events history;
  acknowledge / abandon / release_entry_lock; entries_locked (fail-closed).
  ABANDONED stays monitored and locked; late order -> CONFLICT.
- Automatic resubmission remains disabled.

Tests: round3 21 (15 fail on bb2a2f8; 21 pass); round2 15 pass (1 expectation
changed: unreadable history -> UNRESOLVED, not NOT_SUBMITTED); existing 30 pass.
Timeout hardening and paper-plan corrections remain OPEN. P7-RO proposal added
(read-only, separate from P3); not approved.
